<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Entitlements for the distributed macOS build of the app. Deliberately
	empty, and it has to stay that way.

	The App Sandbox is not a fallback here, it is unsupported. Two reasons,
	either of which is enough: macOS 14.2's Background Task Management
	refuses to let a sandboxed app register an unsandboxed SMAppService job,
	and the reports the app exists to read live in ~/Library/Logs and
	/Library/Logs — outside any container, reachable by an ordinary
	unsandboxed process of the logged-in user and by nothing else. Hardening
	comes from Hardened Runtime (codesign --options runtime) instead.

	The Catalyst build also carries no client entitlement: an iOS-family
	binary holding an entitlement no provisioning profile granted will not
	launch on macOS at all. The macOS branch of PeerAuthenticator
	authenticates by uid and sibling path in its place.

	This file is why the app target must never gain a CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS
	build setting: the device package needs Packaging/Xrash.entitlements and
	this one needs none, and both are applied at signing time by the
	packaging scripts, never by xcodebuild. `make mac-zip-check` fails if
	com.apple.security.app-sandbox appears here.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
